// Where the honeycomb rests on each hook, per raw meat (looks only). Generated by tools/hang/honeyrest3.py and the
// export step in tools/hang (honey_rest3.json); do not edit by hand.
//
// The comb hangs from the hook's smaller curl and gravity takes it as low as the meat lets it, so it hangs down along
// the meat's side or lies along its curve. For each meat on each of the nine hooks, poses around the curl were tried
// (12 ways its flat face can point, tilts of 0 to 90 degrees in 5-degree steps about every level axis in 15-degree
// steps). Kept: those with at most 25 % of the comb inside any meat on a full rack (solid test on a 1 cm grid), or the
// least possible if none is that low, and of those the one whose centre hangs lowest. Some clipping is allowed on
// purpose (the user, test i: "Some clipping is fine. Have it rest along the meat."): the bigger meats cover the curl
// the comb hangs from, and holding it out of the meat entirely made it stick out into the air (test i).
//
// Pose: rotation (x, y, z, w), size (times the copy's own scale) and position, in the rack's own space.
